{"message": "Genuinely? Deep and focused, most of the time. There's something satisfying about staying with a topic long enough to get past the obvious answers — the interesting stuff in any subject tends to sit a layer or two below where a casual conversation naturally stops. When we jump around constantly, I feel like we collect highlights instead of understanding anything.

That said, I don't think the two are opposites. Some of the best conversations wander — but they wander the way a good essay does, where each tangent connects back to something. That's different from channel-surfing, which I find a bit hollow.

So if I had to pick: give me one meaty subject and the patience to dig into it. What's on your mind?"}
